    {
      "id": "44FCuLLxUDVub1H09E4zU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 16687.943369507033,
      "y": -712.3393694775336,
      "width": 1030.7794189453125,
      "height": 1300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 828673907,
      "version": 2460,
      "versionNonce": 2002799044,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790514495096,
      "created": 1790444160410,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Flow 1. \n\nnew event -> get all the rules of each latest week -> create 1 month slot generation\n\nget the event id after created\n\ncreate slots for next 1 month and get the rules if valid show to user if not hide them other slots\n\nlogic for creating slot for 1 month when event is created then\n\n\neventType : interview\nduration in min : 30 minutes\nbuffer before minutes : 10\nbuffer after minutes : 10 \n\nneed to create next 1 month slot objects\n\nTake current date split into year month day\n\nnow take the current Date in yyyy-mm-dd format\n\nlet currenDate = our current date\nlet startTime = 12:00:00 now need iterate over to in terms of minutes wise some kind of loop generation\n                     hh mm ss \n \nminutes can upto 00 to 60 and then after that 12 will become 13 how to work on that generation\n\n\n\nslot generation\n\nget today date and \nday starting timing\n\n\nTodayDate in neutral utc format   :   getTodayDate  in yyyy-mm-dd format \n\n\nstartTime is this date.setMinutes(current + before Minute )\n\ndate.setMinutes( currentMin + 30 minutes )\nendTime is this date.getMinutes( currentMin + after buffer Minutes ) \n\n\njust interate over until its not changed into next month some kind of while loop\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Flow 1. \n\nnew event -> get all the rules of each latest week -> create 1 month slot generation\n\nget the event id after created\n\ncreate slots for next 1 month and get the rules if valid show to user if not hide them other slots\n\nlogic for creating slot for 1 month when event is created then\n\n\neventType : interview\nduration in min : 30 minutes\nbuffer before minutes : 10\nbuffer after minutes : 10 \n\nneed to create next 1 month slot objects\n\nTake current date split into year month day\n\nnow take the current Date in yyyy-mm-dd format\n\nlet currenDate = our current date\nlet startTime = 12:00:00 now need iterate over to in terms of minutes wise some kind of loop generation\n                     hh mm ss \n \nminutes can upto 00 to 60 and then after that 12 will become 13 how to work on that generation\n\n\n\nslot generation\n\nget today date and \nday starting timing\n\n\nTodayDate in neutral utc format   :   getTodayDate  in yyyy-mm-dd format \n\n\nstartTime is this date.setMinutes(current + before Minute )\n\ndate.setMinutes( currentMin + 30 minutes )\nendTime is this date.getMinutes( currentMin + after buffer Minutes ) \n\n\njust interate over until its not changed into next month some kind of while loop\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
