    {
      "id": "SacqYoBsFFHHdsq66lnyC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 16733.88609069771,
      "y": 3303.940154539961,
      "width": 791.988525390625,
      "height": 637.5401277966386,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0n8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 147909254,
      "version": 645,
      "versionNonce": 869638150,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791091913046,
      "created": 1791065342737,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. what if user have 2 rules per same week \n    ex: monday  10:00 to 12:00\n         monday  11:100 to 12:00 man now we needed merge slots to get all rules\n\nsolution : merge slots function will handle\n\nif we can take all the slots per week and we get actual slot timings per week\n            \n2.  if user have two events had same timing slots \n    ex: interview slot :   9th june 9:30 - 10:30\n        resume review slot : 9th june 9:30 - 10:30\n\nHow we overcome that solution : \n\nA interview slot is booked then we need to block or remove this timings \n\n\n3. where are the places we gonna use regenerate slots function  ? \n\n4. if we are creating an event type does this each event type needs to have a\ndifferent rules ?\n\n- nope all event types have single rule but updating it makes slots modified  \n\n",
      "fontSize": 20.40128408949243,
      "baseFontSize": 20.40128408949243,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "S29BW8U8QBXSnZUxKIZZX",
      "originalText": "1. what if user have 2 rules per same week \n    ex: monday  10:00 to 12:00\n         monday  11:100 to 12:00 man now we needed merge slots to get all rules\n\nsolution : merge slots function will handle\n\nif we can take all the slots per week and we get actual slot timings per week\n            \n2.  if user have two events had same timing slots \n    ex: interview slot :   9th june 9:30 - 10:30\n        resume review slot : 9th june 9:30 - 10:30\n\nHow we overcome that solution : \n\nA interview slot is booked then we need to block or remove this timings \n\n\n3. where are the places we gonna use regenerate slots function  ? \n\n4. if we are creating an event type does this each event type needs to have a different rules ?\n\n- nope all event types have single rule but updating it makes slots modified  \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
